Music

00:00:18.097 --> 00:00:19.348
?How are you

00:00:19.557 --> 00:00:21.184
A very ordinary sentence
?Isn’t it

00:00:21.893 --> 00:00:25.897
?When you ask someone how are you
The answer is always clear

00:00:25.897 --> 00:00:27.190
“fine, thank god”

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.817
But if you ask a medical student

00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:32.403
he probably won’t be able to
express his feelings

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.116
This student will not be able to express
What he is going through

00:00:37.658 --> 00:00:42.455
And if we ever think and try to talk to
Someone from outside the college

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:45.374
To tell them about our problems
about our concerns

00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:48.127
They will often tell you 
If you want medicine”

00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:49.796
“then you have to endure it

00:00:49.796 --> 00:00:53.091
This society is not aware of the danger of

00:00:53.091 --> 00:00:55.676
psychological accumulations on
this student

00:00:55.676 --> 00:01:00.932
Several studies have been conducted on
medical students in the USA and Norway

00:01:00.932 --> 00:01:04.769
showed that the ratios of
suicidal thoughts among medical students

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:06.771
ranged between 11% and 23%

00:01:07.605 --> 00:01:12.193
This means that in  all medical schools
in the world, between four people there is

00:01:12.193 --> 00:01:17.240
at least one of them has plans and 
thoughts to commit suicide

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.202
We may not find this thing absurd or 
unreasonable

00:01:21.202 --> 00:01:24.705
Let’s think, an 18 years old student
if we put him

00:01:25.039 --> 00:01:26.707
in some circumstances

00:01:26.707 --> 00:01:28.334
such as isolation from people

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:29.836
away from every thing

00:01:29.836 --> 00:01:31.295
hard conditions for study

00:01:31.295 --> 00:01:33.381
and poor academic attainment in sometimes

00:01:34.006 --> 00:01:37.009
This means that the teaching method
contributes to this

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:39.887
and we have to pay attention to the matter

00:01:39.887 --> 00:01:45.184
We have to pay attention to the teaching
Method influence on this subject

00:01:45.184 --> 00:01:48.688
Now, I was always thinking to make this
change

00:01:49.397 --> 00:01:54.318
but my notion of change and my journy
in it have started in 2012

00:01:54.318 --> 00:01:57.363
when my father passed away after
being admitted to the hospital

00:01:57.363 --> 00:01:59.615
In porpose to have splenectomy

00:01:59.615 --> 00:02:01.659
he died as a result of medical negligence

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:04.787
my father went to this hospital and 
developed acondition known as

00:02:04.787 --> 00:02:08.291
disseminated intravascular coagulation 
or DIC

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:12.170
it means clots in some of body’s arteries

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:16.841
that leads to platelet consumption

00:02:16.924 --> 00:02:20.678
Later, my father went into a coma
and passed away as a result of that

00:02:20.678 --> 00:02:23.472
From there on, a storm hit all of my past

00:02:23.472 --> 00:02:25.975
and made me a new man

00:02:25.975 --> 00:02:28.436
one of his most precious principle
is the change

00:02:28.436 --> 00:02:30.897
To prevent darkness from entering
anew home

00:02:31.105 --> 00:02:33.399
to prevent darkness from
new medical negligence

00:02:33.649 --> 00:02:38.029
I tried to transform all the sadness and
deficit energy to a form of energy

00:02:38.029 --> 00:02:40.573
able to change and make something new

00:02:40.573 --> 00:02:45.369
but when I enter the faculty
I shocked by teaching methods

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.582
which are still in all medical
faculties around the world

00:02:49.624 --> 00:02:55.129
the methods still traditional
it depends only on memorizing and storing

00:02:56.005 --> 00:03:00.593
if I asked you all ,what is
the different between info and knowledge

00:03:00.593 --> 00:03:04.722
what is the different of having info and 
?knowledge

00:03:04.722 --> 00:03:08.809
the info now is for everyone

00:03:08.809 --> 00:03:11.979
medical and technological advances cause

00:03:12.063 --> 00:03:17.860
that the medical info is available for 
everyone, but knowledge is how to use

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:23.407
these info and using these facts
to help people and to make something new

00:03:23.574 --> 00:03:29.872
and to make a change
,but unfortunately this is not followed

00:03:29.872 --> 00:03:32.124
in most of medical faculties around 
the world

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.878
Usually the student is not so employed

00:03:35.878 --> 00:03:39.590
for example, more in treatment

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.760
and not used so much in teaching

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.512
for this reason I talked about

00:03:44.512 --> 00:03:46.264
?how can I make a change

00:03:47.765 --> 00:03:50.184
from this point I start to ask and search

00:03:50.184 --> 00:03:54.480
usually, some university state that you 
should allowed the medical student

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.649
to participat more in patients therapy

00:03:57.149 --> 00:04:00.486
this is something alot of hospitals fear 
from

00:04:00.486 --> 00:04:03.114
fear from medical error

00:04:03.739 --> 00:04:08.119
the surprise was that many studies on  
this topic

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.040
reveal that percentage of error
in teaching hospital are much less

00:04:13.207 --> 00:04:20.172
that because the responsible doctors
are on highly degree of alertness

00:04:20.172 --> 00:04:25.219
so the medical error will be much less
than before

00:04:25.636 --> 00:04:28.973
I am still searching on how can I
make a change

00:04:28.973 --> 00:04:33.853
how can I change
the environment and society I am in

00:04:33.853 --> 00:04:37.315
In my sixth year of study

00:04:37.773 --> 00:04:40.401
at first I created a mini-union

00:04:40.401 --> 00:04:42.445
and its function was like this

00:04:42.445 --> 00:04:47.908
sixth and fifth year students will teach
the students from the fourth year

00:04:47.908 --> 00:04:50.077
wether about clinical information

00:04:50.119 --> 00:04:53.539
or about the medical history
or other aspects

00:04:53.539 --> 00:04:57.335
we finished this course with 
a mini-practical exam for all the students

00:04:57.335 --> 00:04:59.045
there were over sixty students

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:02.256
here was the surprise that I start
to realize

00:05:02.757 --> 00:05:05.593
the students who took apart
in this training all agreed

00:05:05.593 --> 00:05:09.347
that their education level
became higher after this training

00:05:09.805 --> 00:05:13.059
but the most importent point was
in the trainers themselves

00:05:13.059 --> 00:05:15.311
they said that their knowledge inhanced

00:05:15.311 --> 00:05:18.314
they became more confident in themselves

00:05:18.606 --> 00:05:22.401
that’s because the best way to learn
is to teach

00:05:23.402 --> 00:05:25.071
this is why I always

00:05:25.446 --> 00:05:30.910
insist that we should use the students in 
education to make a difference

00:05:31.035 --> 00:05:34.080
to do something bigger
and to improve this subject

00:05:34.705 --> 00:05:39.126
In 2020, and during the quarantine which 
we all been through

00:05:39.502 --> 00:05:42.880
my colleagues and I, one of them is
Laith Azzam

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:45.716
established CLINICS

00:05:45.925 --> 00:05:51.347
Clinics is an institution its purpose was
to change medical education in the country

00:05:51.347 --> 00:05:54.642
I’d like to tell you that until my
standing here on this stage

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:58.229
we have presented more than 350
hours of training

00:05:58.562 --> 00:06:01.190
have been done in different parts of
the country

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.776
we were in Jerusalem, we were in Khalil
in Bethlehem

00:06:03.776 --> 00:06:05.694
in Nablus, in Ramallah
everywhere

00:06:05.694 --> 00:06:08.155
we did a training for most of the students

00:06:09.198 --> 00:06:14.829
on the other hand, I had in this page
students from second, third and fourth

00:06:14.829 --> 00:06:17.873
years who worke on providing medical
content

00:06:17.873 --> 00:06:20.876
they are the ones who contribute in
giving this medical content

00:06:20.876 --> 00:06:24.797
and educating their colleagues 
and educating their friends

00:06:24.797 --> 00:06:27.883
they all agreed on the following things

00:06:27.883 --> 00:06:30.719
first, their confidence in themselves
increased

00:06:31.095 --> 00:06:33.472
their educational attainment became 
greater

00:06:33.472 --> 00:06:36.851
and their confidence in their mental 
health became better

00:06:36.851 --> 00:06:41.105
what I am talking about 
the thing I am trying to convey is

00:06:41.105 --> 00:06:43.941
that to use the students to teach others

00:06:43.941 --> 00:06:47.236
which mean to use the students to 
educate themselves

00:06:47.236 --> 00:06:51.157
this will enhance the psychological
state of all students

00:06:51.157 --> 00:06:54.243
In addition to that, you are giving him
a social value

00:06:54.243 --> 00:06:56.537
a value among all the students
around him

00:06:56.704 --> 00:07:00.708
by doing this, the level of education
will raise up

00:07:01.125 --> 00:07:04.420
the student will stay all the time 
in touch with his knowledge

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.130
all the time in contact with it

00:07:06.422 --> 00:07:09.550
for this, you will also elevate the level
of knowledge

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:15.139
what I am trying to pinpoint is that 
something you can use in all colleges

00:07:15.181 --> 00:07:16.891
not only in medical schools

00:07:17.641 --> 00:07:19.685
we can change the reality

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:24.899
We as young people can change the reality
from every momment in this change

00:07:25.274 --> 00:07:26.275
.Thank you

